{"bendscript":"0.1","blocks":[{"id":"blk-32862","kind":"heading","level":1,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36791","text":"ADR-0005: Deployment Immutability + Active Deployment Pointer Model"}]},{"id":"blk-32863","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32865","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36792","marks":["bold"],"text":"Status:"},{"id":"spn-36793","text":" Accepted (v1)"}]}],"id":"blk-32864","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32867","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36794","marks":["bold"],"text":"Date:"},{"id":"spn-36795","text":" 2026-01-21"}]}],"id":"blk-32866","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32869","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36796","marks":["bold"],"text":"Owners:"},{"id":"spn-36797","text":" webhost.systems engineering"}]}],"id":"blk-32868","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32871","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36798","marks":["bold"],"text":"Related docs:"}]}],"id":"blk-32870","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32873","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36799","marks":["code"],"text":"WebHost.Systems/docs/spec/00_MASTER_SPEC.md"}]}],"id":"blk-32872","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32875","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36800","marks":["code"],"text":"WebHost.Systems/docs/spec/10_API_CONTRACTS.md"}]}],"id":"blk-32874","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32877","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36801","marks":["code"],"text":"WebHost.Systems/docs/spec/20_RUNTIME_PROVIDER_INTERFACE.md"}]}],"id":"blk-32876","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32879","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36802","marks":["code"],"text":"WebHost.Systems/docs/spec/30_DATA_MODEL_CONVEX.md"}]}],"id":"blk-32878","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32881","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36803","marks":["code"],"text":"WebHost.Systems/docs/spec/60_TESTING_ACCEPTANCE.md"}]}],"id":"blk-32880","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32882","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36804","text":"1) Context"}]},{"id":"blk-32883","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36805","text":"webhost.systems deploys untrusted customer agent code to one of multiple runtime providers and routes invocations to the correct deployed version. The platform must support:"}]},{"id":"blk-32884","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32886","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36806","text":"safe, repeatable deployments,"}]}],"id":"blk-32885","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32888","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36807","text":"rapid iteration with reliable rollbacks,"}]}],"id":"blk-32887","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32890","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36808","text":"clear auditability (“what is running now, and who changed it?”),"}]}],"id":"blk-32889","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32892","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36809","text":"consistent routing across multiple runtime providers,"}]}],"id":"blk-32891","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32894","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36810","text":"robust handling of partial failures (deploy succeeded on provider but DB update failed; or vice versa),"}]}],"id":"blk-32893","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32896","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36811","text":"deterministic metering attribution to "},{"id":"spn-36812","marks":["code"],"text":"{userId, agentId, deploymentId, runtimeProvider}"},{"id":"spn-36813","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-32895","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32897","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36814","text":"Early prototypes often store deployment state “in place” on the agent record (e.g., overwriting "},{"id":"spn-36815","marks":["code"],"text":"workerUrl"},{"id":"spn-36816","text":", updating "},{"id":"spn-36817","marks":["code"],"text":"codeHash"},{"id":"spn-36818","text":", etc.). This tends to create correctness and support problems:"}]},{"id":"blk-32898","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32900","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36819","text":"You lose historical context (“what changed?”)."}]}],"id":"blk-32899","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32902","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36820","text":"Rollback is difficult or impossible without redeploying."}]}],"id":"blk-32901","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32904","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36821","text":"In-flight deploys can corrupt the “current” state if they fail midway."}]}],"id":"blk-32903","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32906","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36822","text":"Auditing, debugging, and cost reconciliation become fragile."}]}],"id":"blk-32905","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32908","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36823","text":"Concurrency introduces race conditions: two deploys can interleave and leave the agent in an inconsistent state."}]}],"id":"blk-32907","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32909","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36824","text":"Therefore, the system needs a durable, auditable, and concurrency-tolerant model for deployments and routing."}]},{"id":"blk-32910","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36825","text":"2) Decision"}]},{"id":"blk-32911","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36826","text":"2.1 Deployment immutability"}]},{"id":"blk-32912","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36827","text":"A "},{"id":"spn-36828","marks":["bold"],"text":"Deployment"},{"id":"spn-36829","text":" is an immutable record representing a specific released version of an agent."}]},{"id":"blk-32913","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32915","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36830","text":"A new deployment attempt MUST create a "},{"id":"spn-36831","marks":["bold"],"text":"new deployment record"},{"id":"spn-36832","text":" ("},{"id":"spn-36833","marks":["code"],"text":"deployments"},{"id":"spn-36834","text":" table row)."}]}],"id":"blk-32914","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32917","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36835","text":"Deployment records MUST be treated as immutable after creation, except for a narrowly defined mutable subset:"}]}],"id":"blk-32916","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32919","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36836","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-36837","text":" (e.g., deploying → active/failed)"}]}],"id":"blk-32918","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32921","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36838","marks":["code"],"text":"providerRef"},{"id":"spn-36839","text":" (filled once known)"}]}],"id":"blk-32920","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32923","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36840","marks":["code"],"text":"errorMessage"},{"id":"spn-36841","text":" (sanitized)"}]}],"id":"blk-32922","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32925","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36842","text":"timestamps like "},{"id":"spn-36843","marks":["code"],"text":"deployedAtMs"},{"id":"spn-36844","text":" / "},{"id":"spn-36845","marks":["code"],"text":"finishedAtMs"}]}],"id":"blk-32924","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32927","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36846","text":"optional "},{"id":"spn-36847","marks":["code"],"text":"logsRef"},{"id":"spn-36848","text":" pointer"}]}],"id":"blk-32926","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32929","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36849","text":"Any new code/artifact/provider configuration change MUST create a new deployment record (never modify an existing deployment to “become” the new version)."}]}],"id":"blk-32928","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32930","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36850","text":"2.2 Active deployment pointer"}]},{"id":"blk-32931","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36851","text":"Each agent has a single routing pointer:"}]},{"id":"blk-32932","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32934","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36852","marks":["code"],"text":"agents.activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-36853","text":" points to the deployment that should receive invocations."}]}],"id":"blk-32933","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32936","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36854","text":"Rollback (and “activate old deployment”) is implemented by updating "},{"id":"spn-36855","marks":["code"],"text":"agents.activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-36856","text":" to a previous deployment id."}]}],"id":"blk-32935","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32938","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36857","text":"Invocation routing uses ONLY:"}]}],"id":"blk-32937","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32940","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36858","text":"agent ownership checks + status checks, then"}]}],"id":"blk-32939","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32942","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36859","marks":["code"],"text":"activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-36860","text":" → "},{"id":"spn-36861","marks":["code"],"text":"deployments.providerRef"},{"id":"spn-36862","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-36863","marks":["code"],"text":"deployments.runtimeProvider"},{"id":"spn-36864","text":" to select runtime adapter and invoke."}]}],"id":"blk-32941","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32943","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36865","text":"2.3 Single-writer rule per agent during deploy (v1 simplification)"}]},{"id":"blk-32944","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36866","text":"To reduce complexity and prevent version races in v1:"}]},{"id":"blk-32945","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32947","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36867","text":"The platform MUST prevent concurrent deployments per agent (e.g., guard with "},{"id":"spn-36868","marks":["code"],"text":"agents.status=deploying"},{"id":"spn-36869","text":" or a server-side mutex mechanism)."}]}],"id":"blk-32946","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32949","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36870","text":"A second deploy attempt while "},{"id":"spn-36871","marks":["code"],"text":"deploying"},{"id":"spn-36872","text":" SHOULD fail with "},{"id":"spn-36873","marks":["code"],"text":"CONFLICT"},{"id":"spn-36874","text":" (or be queued post-v1)."}]}],"id":"blk-32948","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32950","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36875","text":"3) Rationale"}]},{"id":"blk-32951","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36876","text":"3.1 Safety and correctness"}]},{"id":"blk-32952","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36877","text":"Immutability avoids a class of “torn writes” where partial updates leave the system in an inconsistent state. If deployment artifacts and references are immutable, you can always answer:"}]},{"id":"blk-32953","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32955","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36878","text":"exactly what was deployed,"}]}],"id":"blk-32954","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32957","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36879","text":"where it was deployed,"}]}],"id":"blk-32956","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32959","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36880","text":"and when it changed."}]}],"id":"blk-32958","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32960","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36881","text":"3.2 Rollbacks become fast and reliable"}]},{"id":"blk-32961","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36882","text":"With immutable deployments, rollback is primarily a pointer change:"}]},{"id":"blk-32962","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32964","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36883","text":"no redeploy required (unless provider forces it for technical reasons),"}]}],"id":"blk-32963","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32966","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36884","text":"quick recovery from bad deploys,"}]}],"id":"blk-32965","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32968","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36885","text":"repeatable and auditable."}]}],"id":"blk-32967","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32969","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36886","text":"3.3 Auditing and supportability"}]},{"id":"blk-32970","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36887","text":"A permanent deployment history supports:"}]},{"id":"blk-32971","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32973","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36888","text":"customer support (“what changed?”),"}]}],"id":"blk-32972","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32975","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36889","text":"incident response (“who activated what?”),"}]}],"id":"blk-32974","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32977","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36890","text":"compliance-aligned audits."}]}],"id":"blk-32976","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32978","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36891","text":"3.4 Metering attribution and future cost reconciliation"}]},{"id":"blk-32979","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36892","text":"When telemetry references a "},{"id":"spn-36893","marks":["code"],"text":"deploymentId"},{"id":"spn-36894","text":" and deployments are immutable, usage can always be attributed to an exact version and provider resource set. This also enables future provider cost reconciliation by tagging provider resources per deployment."}]},{"id":"blk-32980","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36895","text":"3.5 Multi-runtime routing simplicity"}]},{"id":"blk-32981","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36896","text":"A single "},{"id":"spn-36897","marks":["code"],"text":"activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-36898","text":" model works uniformly across providers:"}]},{"id":"blk-32982","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32984","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36899","text":"Cloudflare: "},{"id":"spn-36900","marks":["code"],"text":"providerRef.cloudflare.workerUrl"},{"id":"spn-36901","text":" etc."}]}],"id":"blk-32983","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32986","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36902","text":"AgentCore: "},{"id":"spn-36903","marks":["code"],"text":"providerRef.agentcore.agentRuntimeArn"},{"id":"spn-36904","text":" etc."}]}],"id":"blk-32985","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32987","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36905","text":"The control plane remains provider-agnostic; provider-specific details are confined to adapter implementations."}]},{"id":"blk-32988","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36906","text":"4) Alternatives considered"}]},{"id":"blk-32989","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36907","text":"A) Mutable deployment state stored on the agent row only"}]},{"id":"blk-32990","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36908","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pros"}]},{"id":"blk-32991","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32993","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36909","text":"Minimal schema."}]}],"id":"blk-32992","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32995","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36910","text":"Simplifies “what’s currently active” (single record)."}]}],"id":"blk-32994","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-32996","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36911","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cons"}]},{"id":"blk-32997","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-32999","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36912","text":"Loses history."}]}],"id":"blk-32998","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33001","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36913","text":"Hard to rollback."}]}],"id":"blk-33000","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33003","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36914","text":"Partial failures can corrupt the running pointer."}]}],"id":"blk-33002","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33005","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36915","text":"Difficult to audit and debug."}]}],"id":"blk-33004","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33007","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36916","text":"Makes telemetry attribution ambiguous when “current deployment” changes."}]}],"id":"blk-33006","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33008","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36917","marks":["bold"],"text":"Decision:"},{"id":"spn-36918","text":" Rejected."}]},{"id":"blk-33009","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36919","text":"B) Immutable deployments without an active pointer (derive “active” from latest successful deploy)"}]},{"id":"blk-33010","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36920","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pros"}]},{"id":"blk-33011","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33013","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36921","text":"No pointer updates; “active” is last successful deployment."}]}],"id":"blk-33012","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33014","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36922","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cons"}]},{"id":"blk-33015","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33017","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36923","text":"Rollback becomes non-trivial (must “fake” a new deploy or add flags)."}]}],"id":"blk-33016","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33019","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36924","text":"“Latest” is not always what you want running (e.g., canary, manual pinning)."}]}],"id":"blk-33018","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33021","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36925","text":"In-flight deploys complicate “latest success” semantics."}]}],"id":"blk-33020","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33022","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36926","marks":["bold"],"text":"Decision:"},{"id":"spn-36927","text":" Rejected."}]},{"id":"blk-33023","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36928","text":"C) Mutable “active deployment” record plus separate immutable history"}]},{"id":"blk-33024","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36929","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pros"}]},{"id":"blk-33025","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33027","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36930","text":"A dedicated active record could simplify reads."}]}],"id":"blk-33026","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33028","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36931","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cons"}]},{"id":"blk-33029","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33031","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36932","text":"You now have two sources of truth to keep consistent."}]}],"id":"blk-33030","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33033","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36933","text":"Reintroduces mutability issues for the “active” record."}]}],"id":"blk-33032","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33035","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36934","text":"Added complexity with limited benefit over a pointer."}]}],"id":"blk-33034","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33036","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36935","marks":["bold"],"text":"Decision:"},{"id":"spn-36936","text":" Rejected."}]},{"id":"blk-33037","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36937","text":"D) Blue/green or canary routing model as default"}]},{"id":"blk-33038","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36938","marks":["bold"],"text":"Pros"}]},{"id":"blk-33039","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33041","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36939","text":"Advanced rollout safety."}]}],"id":"blk-33040","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33042","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36940","marks":["bold"],"text":"Cons"}]},{"id":"blk-33043","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33045","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36941","text":"Too complex for v1."}]}],"id":"blk-33044","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33047","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36942","text":"Requires traffic splitting, per-request routing policies, and richer metrics gating."}]}],"id":"blk-33046","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33049","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36943","text":"Still requires immutable deployments underneath."}]}],"id":"blk-33048","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33050","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36944","marks":["bold"],"text":"Decision:"},{"id":"spn-36945","text":" Deferred to post-v1; can be built on top of this ADR."}]},{"id":"blk-33051","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36946","text":"5) Consequences"}]},{"id":"blk-33052","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36947","text":"5.1 Positive consequences"}]},{"id":"blk-33053","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33055","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36948","text":"Reliable rollback (pointer flip)."}]}],"id":"blk-33054","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33057","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36949","text":"Clear deployment audit trail."}]}],"id":"blk-33056","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33059","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36950","text":"Strong basis for incident response and debugging."}]}],"id":"blk-33058","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33061","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36951","text":"Simplified multi-runtime invocation routing."}]}],"id":"blk-33060","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33063","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36952","text":"Enables deterministic telemetry attribution and later cost reconciliation."}]}],"id":"blk-33062","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33064","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36953","text":"5.2 Negative consequences / tradeoffs"}]},{"id":"blk-33065","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33067","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36954","text":"More schema and records (deployments grow over time)."}]}],"id":"blk-33066","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33069","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36955","text":"Requires retention policy decisions for old deployments (storage cleanup, provider resource deprovisioning)."}]}],"id":"blk-33068","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33071","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36956","text":"Requires careful handling of “deploy succeeded but DB update failed” and vice versa."}]}],"id":"blk-33070","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33073","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36957","text":"Requires a versioning strategy (monotonic per agent) and concurrency controls."}]}],"id":"blk-33072","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33074","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36958","text":"6) Implementation details (normative requirements)"}]},{"id":"blk-33075","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36959","text":"6.1 Data model requirements"}]},{"id":"blk-33076","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36960","text":"The following fields/semantics MUST exist (names may vary if consistent):"}]},{"id":"blk-33077","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33079","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36961","marks":["code"],"text":"deployments"},{"id":"spn-36962","text":" table with:"}]}],"id":"blk-33078","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33081","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36963","marks":["code"],"text":"agentId"},{"id":"spn-36964","text":", "},{"id":"spn-36965","marks":["code"],"text":"userId"}]}],"id":"blk-33080","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33083","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36966","marks":["code"],"text":"version"},{"id":"spn-36967","text":" (monotonic per agent)"}]}],"id":"blk-33082","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33085","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36968","marks":["code"],"text":"runtimeProvider"}]}],"id":"blk-33084","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33087","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36969","marks":["code"],"text":"artifact"},{"id":"spn-36970","text":" reference (uploaded bundle or repo ref)"}]}],"id":"blk-33086","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33089","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36971","marks":["code"],"text":"providerRef"},{"id":"spn-36972","text":" (runtime-specific invoke reference)"}]}],"id":"blk-33088","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33091","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36973","marks":["code"],"text":"status"},{"id":"spn-36974","text":" and "},{"id":"spn-36975","marks":["code"],"text":"errorMessage"}]}],"id":"blk-33090","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33093","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36976","text":"timestamps ("},{"id":"spn-36977","marks":["code"],"text":"createdAtMs"},{"id":"spn-36978","text":", "},{"id":"spn-36979","marks":["code"],"text":"deployedAtMs"},{"id":"spn-36980","text":", "},{"id":"spn-36981","marks":["code"],"text":"finishedAtMs"},{"id":"spn-36982","text":")"}]}],"id":"blk-33092","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33095","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36983","marks":["code"],"text":"agents.activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-36984","text":" pointer to "},{"id":"spn-36985","marks":["code"],"text":"deployments._id"},{"id":"spn-36986","text":" (nullable)"}]}],"id":"blk-33094","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33096","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-36987","text":"6.2 Immutability enforcement"}]},{"id":"blk-33097","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33099","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36988","text":"Server code MUST NOT update artifact identity fields on "},{"id":"spn-36989","marks":["code"],"text":"deployments"},{"id":"spn-36990","text":" after creation:"}]}],"id":"blk-33098","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33101","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36991","marks":["code"],"text":"artifact.*"},{"id":"spn-36992","text":", "},{"id":"spn-36993","marks":["code"],"text":"manifest.*"},{"id":"spn-36994","text":", "},{"id":"spn-36995","marks":["code"],"text":"runtimeProvider"},{"id":"spn-36996","text":", "},{"id":"spn-36997","marks":["code"],"text":"version"}]}],"id":"blk-33100","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33103","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36998","text":"Only the allowed mutable subset may be updated (status/providerRef/error/timestamps/log pointers)."}]}],"id":"blk-33102","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33105","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-36999","text":"Client code MUST NOT be allowed to update deployment rows directly."}]}],"id":"blk-33104","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33106","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37000","text":"6.3 Activation rules"}]},{"id":"blk-33107","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37001","text":"When activating a deployment (including rollback):"}]},{"id":"blk-33108","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33110","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37002","text":"The target deployment MUST:"}]}],"id":"blk-33109","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33112","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37003","text":"belong to the agent,"}]}],"id":"blk-33111","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33114","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37004","text":"belong to the current user (tenant check),"}]}],"id":"blk-33113","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33116","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37005","text":"be in a valid state for activation (recommended: "},{"id":"spn-37006","marks":["code"],"text":"status=active"},{"id":"spn-37007","text":")."}]}],"id":"blk-33115","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33118","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37008","text":"The system MUST update "},{"id":"spn-37009","marks":["code"],"text":"agents.activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-37010","text":" to the target deployment id."}]}],"id":"blk-33117","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33120","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37011","text":"The system SHOULD record an audit log entry:"}]}],"id":"blk-33119","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33122","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37012","marks":["code"],"text":"deployment.activate"},{"id":"spn-37013","text":" with "},{"id":"spn-37014","marks":["code"],"text":"{agentId, deploymentId}"},{"id":"spn-37015","text":" and optional reason."}]}],"id":"blk-33121","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33123","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37016","text":"6.4 Routing rules"}]},{"id":"blk-33124","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37017","text":"The invocation gateway MUST route using: 1. resolve agent and enforce ownership (unless public agents exist post-v1), 2. verify agent is not "},{"id":"spn-37018","marks":["code"],"text":"disabled"},{"id":"spn-37019","text":"/deleted, 3. read "},{"id":"spn-37020","marks":["code"],"text":"activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-37021","text":", 4. load deployment by id and verify it belongs to agent and user, 5. route via runtime adapter selected by "},{"id":"spn-37022","marks":["code"],"text":"deployment.runtimeProvider"},{"id":"spn-37023","text":", 6. invoke using "},{"id":"spn-37024","marks":["code"],"text":"deployment.providerRef"},{"id":"spn-37025","text":"."}]},{"id":"blk-33125","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37026","text":"Routing MUST NOT use “latest deployment” heuristics."}]},{"id":"blk-33126","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37027","text":"6.5 Deploy flow atomicity and failure handling"}]},{"id":"blk-33127","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37028","text":"A deployment flow typically spans multiple systems (DB + provider). The platform MUST handle partial failures."}]},{"id":"blk-33128","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37029","text":"Minimum v1 requirement:"}]},{"id":"blk-33129","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33131","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37030","text":"The system MUST persist a deployment row with "},{"id":"spn-37031","marks":["code"],"text":"status=deploying"},{"id":"spn-37032","text":" before making provider calls."}]}],"id":"blk-33130","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33133","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37033","text":"If provider deployment fails:"}]}],"id":"blk-33132","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33135","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37034","text":"set deployment "},{"id":"spn-37035","marks":["code"],"text":"status=failed"},{"id":"spn-37036","text":" and store sanitized "},{"id":"spn-37037","marks":["code"],"text":"errorMessage"},{"id":"spn-37038","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-33134","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33137","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37039","text":"set agent "},{"id":"spn-37040","marks":["code"],"text":"status=error"},{"id":"spn-37041","text":" (or keep existing status but expose failure)."}]}],"id":"blk-33136","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33139","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37042","text":"If provider deployment succeeds but DB update fails:"}]}],"id":"blk-33138","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33141","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37043","text":"the system MUST have a retry mechanism (manual or automated) to reconcile:"}]}],"id":"blk-33140","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33143","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37044","text":"either re-run the “finalize deploy” step idempotently, or"}]}],"id":"blk-33142","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33145","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37045","text":"detect orphaned provider resources via tags and mark deployment active later."}]}],"id":"blk-33144","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33147","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37046","text":"If DB update succeeds but provider deployment later fails (rare but possible due to eventual consistency):"}]}],"id":"blk-33146","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33149","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37047","text":"system must reconcile on next healthcheck/invoke attempt and mark deployment failed if unusable."}]}],"id":"blk-33148","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33150","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37048","text":"6.6 Provider resource tagging (required for cleanup and reconciliation)"}]},{"id":"blk-33151","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37049","text":"All provider resources created for a deployment MUST be tagged/labelled with:"}]},{"id":"blk-33152","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33154","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37050","marks":["code"],"text":"userId"}]}],"id":"blk-33153","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33156","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37051","marks":["code"],"text":"agentId"}]}],"id":"blk-33155","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33158","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37052","marks":["code"],"text":"deploymentId"}]}],"id":"blk-33157","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33160","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37053","marks":["code"],"text":"deploymentVersion"}]}],"id":"blk-33159","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33162","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37054","marks":["code"],"text":"runtimeProvider"}]}],"id":"blk-33161","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33163","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37055","text":"6.7 Retention and cleanup"}]},{"id":"blk-33164","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33166","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37056","text":"Deployments are retained as part of audit history."}]}],"id":"blk-33165","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33168","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37057","text":"The platform SHOULD implement:"}]}],"id":"blk-33167","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33170","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37058","text":"retention policy for old deployments (e.g., keep last N or last X days) per tier,"}]}],"id":"blk-33169","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33172","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37059","text":"best-effort deprovisioning of provider resources when deployments are deleted or when an agent is deleted."}]}],"id":"blk-33171","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33174","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37060","text":"Cleanup MUST be careful not to remove resources for the currently active deployment."}]}],"id":"blk-33173","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33175","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37061","text":"7) Testing requirements (acceptance-focused)"}]},{"id":"blk-33176","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37062","text":"7.1 Unit tests (MUST)"}]},{"id":"blk-33177","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33179","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37063","text":"Deployment status transition validation."}]}],"id":"blk-33178","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33181","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37064","text":"Immutability enforcement (attempted mutation of immutable fields rejected)."}]}],"id":"blk-33180","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33183","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37065","text":"Activation validation (wrong agent/user/state rejected)."}]}],"id":"blk-33182","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33185","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37066","text":"Routing resolver uses "},{"id":"spn-37067","marks":["code"],"text":"activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-37068","text":" only."}]}],"id":"blk-33184","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33186","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37069","text":"7.2 Integration tests (MUST)"}]},{"id":"blk-33187","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33189","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37070","text":"Deploy creates new immutable record; a second deploy creates a second record."}]}],"id":"blk-33188","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33191","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37071","text":"Activate (rollback) changes routing immediately."}]}],"id":"blk-33190","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33193","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37072","text":"Concurrent deploy attempts are rejected with "},{"id":"spn-37073","marks":["code"],"text":"CONFLICT"},{"id":"spn-37074","text":" (v1)."}]}],"id":"blk-33192","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33195","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37075","text":"Telemetry attribution includes correct "},{"id":"spn-37076","marks":["code"],"text":"deploymentId"},{"id":"spn-37077","text":"."}]}],"id":"blk-33194","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33196","kind":"heading","level":3,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37078","text":"7.3 E2E tests (MUST)"}]},{"id":"blk-33197","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33199","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37079","text":"Deploy v1 → invoke returns v1 output."}]}],"id":"blk-33198","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33201","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37080","text":"Deploy v2 → invoke returns v2 output."}]}],"id":"blk-33200","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33203","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37081","text":"Activate v1 → invoke returns v1 output again."}]}],"id":"blk-33202","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33205","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37082","text":"Deployment history remains intact and visible."}]}],"id":"blk-33204","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33206","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37083","text":"8) Future extensions enabled by this ADR"}]},{"id":"blk-33207","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37084","text":"This model is a foundation for:"}]},{"id":"blk-33208","items":[{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33210","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37085","text":"canary/blue-green deployments (multiple “active” pointers with traffic split policies),"}]}],"id":"blk-33209","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33212","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37086","text":"environment promotion (dev → staging → prod) with deployment immutability preserved,"}]}],"id":"blk-33211","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33214","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37087","text":"signed deployment manifests / provenance,"}]}],"id":"blk-33213","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33216","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37088","text":"provider billing reconciliation (resource tags + immutable providerRef),"}]}],"id":"blk-33215","kind":"list-item"},{"blocks":[{"id":"blk-33218","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37089","text":"more advanced rollback policies (automatic rollback on error rate thresholds)."}]}],"id":"blk-33217","kind":"list-item"}],"kind":"list","ordered":false},{"id":"blk-33219","kind":"heading","level":2,"spans":[{"id":"spn-37090","text":"9) Acceptance criteria"}]},{"id":"blk-33220","kind":"paragraph","spans":[{"id":"spn-37091","text":"This ADR is correctly implemented when: 1. Every deployment attempt creates a new deployment record and does not mutate previous deployments’ immutable fields. 2. An agent’s invocations always route to "},{"id":"spn-37092","marks":["code"],"text":"activeDeploymentId"},{"id":"spn-37093","text":" (no “latest deploy” routing). 3. Rollback is implemented as an activation/pointer update and takes effect immediately for new invocations. 4. Deployment status transitions are correct and failures do not corrupt the active deployment pointer. 5. Provider resources are tagged with "},{"id":"spn-37094","marks":["code"],"text":"{userId, agentId, deploymentId}"},{"id":"spn-37095","text":". 6. E2E tests demonstrate deploy v1 → deploy v2 → rollback to v1 with correct outputs and preserved history."}]}],"edges":[],"id":"bagaaiera2edbrji6gwvppfegjmy6euxam7e466xslbtvcc6qqvvjoyy3piha","vocabulary":"ampersand.docs.fs.v1"}